==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|habuch}}, {{m|goh|habuh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*habukaz}}, probably ultimately derived from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||seize}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|havik}}, Low German {{m|nds|Haavk}}, English {{m|en|hawk}}, Swedish {{m|sv|hök}}, Norwegian {{m|no|hauk}}.

